      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "1. We tried H&M&L and it has similar performance than H&L. Probably 2-3 levels are sufficient\n2. As the segment number depends on latent state (e.g. more compute for hard problem, less for simpler ones), we need a policy function $\\pi(z_t) \\mapsto \\{ halt, continue\\}$. Deep Q-learning is a simple solution, there're definitely more efficient RL methods to explore. Hyperparameter optimization methods are not state-dependent.",
